Title: Search Algorithm and Iterative Deepening | official-stockfish/Stockfish | DeepWiki
URL: https://deepwiki.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/4.1-search-algorithm-and-iterative-deepening
Published: N/A
Author: N/A
Highlights:
This document covers the core search algorithm implementation in Stockfish, focusing on the iterative deepening framework and the main alpha-beta search function. It describes how the engine progressively searches deeper until time runs out, how nodes are explored using alpha-beta pruning, and the various search optimizations including extensions, reductions, and pruning heuristics.

For parallel search coordination and thread management, see Thread Management and Parallel Search. For move ordering details, see Move Ordering and Move Picker. For the evaluation of leaf positions, see NNUE Neural Network Evaluation. For time management decisions, see Time Management.
...
Stockfish implements a sophisticated alpha-beta search with iterative deepening. The main search entry point for a thread is `Search::Worker::start_searching()`, which initializes the search and calls `iterative_deepening()`. The search progresses depth-by-depth, using results from shallower depths to improve deeper searches through move ordering and aspiration windows.
...
| Component | Function/Class | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Iterative Deepening | `Search::Worker::iterative_deepening()` | Main loop that searches increasing depths |
| Alpha-Beta Search | `Search::Worker::search ()` | Recursive negamax search with pruning |
| Quiescence Search | `Search::Worker::qsearch ()` | Tactical search at leaf nodes |
| Search Stack | `Search::Stack` | Per-ply context and history pointers |
| Root Moves | `Search::RootMoves` | Principal variation tracking at the root |
...
_deepening()`
...
The `search ()` function is the heart of the engine, implementing negamax search with alpha-beta pruning. It is a template function parameterized by `NodeType` (`Root`, `PV`, or `NonPV`).
...
| Node Type | Characteristics | Search Window | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Root` | Top-level node | Full `[alpha, beta]` | Searches all root moves, maintains full PV |
| `PV` | Principal Variation | Full `[alpha, beta]` | Nodes expected to produce best moves |
| `NonPV` | Non-PV nodes | Null window `[beta-1, beta]` | Faster search for non-critical nodes |
...
Quiescence search (`qsearch`) extends the main search at leaf nodes by searching tactical moves (captures and checks) until a "quiet" position is reached. This prevents the horizon effect where the evaluation misses immediate tactical sequences.
...
1. Stand Pat: If not in check, the static evaluation establishes a lower bound (can always choose not to capture) src/search.cpp 1538-1544
2. Futility Pruning: If `futilityBase + captured_piece_value <= alpha`, the capture is pruned src/search.cpp 1598-1612
3. SEE Pruning: Moves that lose material according to Static Exchange Evaluation are skipped src/search.cpp 1614-1615
4. Check Extensions: When in check, evasions are searched src/search.cpp 1526-1527
...
If evaluation is far below alpha at shallow depth, drop into quiescence search src/search.cpp 870-874
...
If evaluation exceeds beta by a margin at shallow depth, return early src/search.cpp 876-890
...
Stockfish uses correction history to adjust static evaluations based on search results. It stores learned adjustments for pawn, minor, and non-pawn configurations.
...
The `correction_value` function combines various history components to adjust the raw static evaluation src/search.cpp 84-100

